#: 2ec11c86f2924d64907051de9fd5a2af
msgid "Explanation"
msgstr ""

#: b99c264ad5314bb884769cf9338ced6d
msgid ""
"Explanation is a discursive treatment of a subject, that permits "
"*reflection*. Explanation is **understanding-oriented**."
msgstr ""

#: e37cb70c43ea40c2a99d298b568ed364
msgid ""
"Explanation deepens and broadens the reader's understanding of a subject."
" It brings clarity, light and context."
msgstr ""

#: 8475420fccef46919a2fcd39d660a859
msgid ""
"Explanation - understanding oriented, theoretical knowledge, that serves "
"our study"
msgstr ""

#: 070b28f68ba54a9eb46e01e582c232f6
msgid ""
"The concept of *reflection* is important. Reflection occurs *after* "
"something else, and depends on something else, yet at the same time "
"brings something new - shines a new light - on the subject matter."
msgstr ""

#: c26c0f544855449781fd59a2878f7d91
msgid ""
"The perspective of explanation is higher and wider than that of the other"
" three types. It does not take the user's eye-level view, as in a how-to "
"guide, or a close-up view of the machinery, like reference material. Its "
"scope in each case is a topic - \"an area of knowledge\", that somehow "
"has to be bounded in a reasonable, meaningful way."
msgstr ""

#: 4020becfa1ae40ee933aed3e293e2717
msgid ""
"For the user, explanation joins things together. It's an answer to the "
"question: *Can you tell me about ...?*"
msgstr ""

#: 25f5d2bf3fe04c98b607b1b7bb2dcb67
msgid ""
"It's documentation that it makes sense to read while away from the "
"product itself (one could say, explanation is the only kind of "
"documentation that it might make sense to read in the bath)."
msgstr ""

#: 574c1fff9dd444b5b0635261833708af
msgid "The value and place of explanation"
msgstr ""

#: f314cbbc482542fab2034be64d3d3ec4
msgid "Explanation and understanding"
msgstr ""

#: b6b6c002df4c4c519f7fbe6e79555ad6
msgid ""
"Explanation  is characterised by its distance from the active concerns of"
" the practitioner. It doesn't have direct implications for what they do, "
"or for their work. This means that it's sometimes seen as being of lesser"
" importance. That's a mistake; it may be less *urgent* than the other "
"three, but it's no less *important*. It's not a luxury. No practitioner "
"of a craft can afford to be without an understanding of that craft, and "
"needs the explanatory material that will help weave it together."
msgstr ""

#: e64f1d0b64c34415bbad60c5b306a42c
msgid ""
"Your explanation documentation doesn't need to be called *Explanation*. "
"Alternatives include:"
msgstr ""

#: eea813cf28f64bfbbe62411b03236058
msgid "*Discussion*"
msgstr ""

#: 6b4cfa1e0d3b49ddbf248b20cf1981e0
msgid "*Background*"
msgstr ""

#: 9d1276d1f9ed4431b35c0c6419207591
msgid "*Conceptual guides*"
msgstr ""

#: 27478e699ede430aaeea3bbfba7d1e0c
msgid "*Topics*"
msgstr ""

#: 10fbddcee7634a87ae5ef05cb3b05dff
msgid ""
"The word *explanation* - and its cognates in other languages - refer to "
"*unfolding*, the revelation of what is hidden in the folds. So "
"explanation brings to the light things that were implicit or obscured."
msgstr ""

#: 1ca411424f884148aff6145a623df031
msgid ""
"Similarly, words that mean *understanding* share roots in words meaning "
"to hold or grasp (as in *comprehend*). That's an important part of "
"understanding, to be able to hold something or be in possession of it. "
"Understanding seals together the other components of our mastery of a "
"craft, and makes it safely our own."
msgstr ""

#: a9570a917dc44d70a48f56776517da82
msgid ""
"Understanding doesn't *come from* explanation, but explanation is "
"required to form that web that helps hold everything together. Without "
"it, the practitioner's knowledge of their craft is loose and fragmented "
"and fragile, and their exercise of it is *anxious*."
msgstr ""

#: dee7b8ec0add481f8b21a203cf784dec
msgid "Explanation and its boundaries"
msgstr ""

#: 718f917508b649fb9cbf74db4ccf2039
msgid ""
"Quite often explanation is not explicitly recognised in documentation; "
"and the idea that things need to be explained is often only faintly "
"expressed. Instead, explanation tends to be scattered in small parcels in"
" other sections."
msgstr ""

#: 836ecb1d22764bd1af40461fc82452cd
msgid ""
"It's not always easy to write good explanatory material. Where does one "
"start? It's also not clear where to conclude. There is an open-endedness "
"about it that can give the writer too many possibilities."
msgstr ""

#: 6e108fbdae2c46b0adb7605f632209e3
msgid ""
"Tutorials, how-to-guides and reference are all clearly defined in their "
"scope by something that is also well-defined: by what you need the user "
"to learn, what task the user needs to achieve, or just by the scope of "
"the machine itself."
msgstr ""

#: 00c563578af64b0bbd5c7b97dfdff3bb
msgid ""
"In the case of explanation, it's useful to have a real or imagined *why* "
"question to serve as a prompt. Otherwise, you simply have to draw some "
"lines that mark out a reasonable area and be satisfied with that."
msgstr ""

#: 853649e00f8f4ab79aac41c1e0a1ee99
msgid "Writing good explanation"
msgstr ""

#: be044afb681c4513b7a1966dbce6baa7
msgid "Make connections"
msgstr ""

#: bae037875f2b4477a3ef7bf80efb00d7
msgid ""
"When writing explanation you are helping to weave a web of understanding "
"for your readers. **Make connections** to other things, even to things "
"outside the immediate topic, if that helps."
msgstr ""

#: bfd0e4e52b27431a8fad5403d72ac0ef
msgid "Provide context"
msgstr ""

#: f90977860e164f5d8bb6ff711e79b16c
msgid ""
"**Provide background and context in your explanation**: explain *why* "
"things are so - design decisions, historical reasons, technical "
"constraints - draw implications, mention specific examples."
msgstr ""

#: 6e52d5ff836d4f5cb46e497788797237
msgid "Talk *about* the subject"
msgstr ""

#: 100772f7a48a4c26a1fb3db050ff29e9
msgid "the bigger picture"
msgstr ""

#: c6c44d2be0664bbebaeb8f3d72646e0f
msgid "history"
msgstr ""

#: 694baa0e4a4c4fd19fe6cead033ff99a
msgid "choices, alternatives, possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: 4749e2626db74b68ac1b19a7a2c9d957
msgid "why: reasons and justifications"
msgstr ""

#: 023898eaae174668b09c8c68e52c4bcb
msgid ""
"Explanation guides are *about* a topic in the sense that they are "
"*around* it. Even the names of your explanation guides should reflect "
"this; you should be able to place an implicit (or even explicit) *about* "
"in front of each title. For example: *About user authentication*, or "
"*About database connection policies*."
msgstr ""

#: 83cc6a73df2f4e1db9e94f1665e46e0a
msgid "Admit opinion and perspective"
msgstr ""

#: 936922c469204a84bcc97b42420ac8c4
msgid ""
"Opinion might seem like a funny thing to introduce into documentation. "
"The fact is that all human activity and knowledge is invested within "
"opinion, with beliefs and thoughts. The reality of any human creation is "
"rich with opinion, and that needs to be part of any understanding of it."
msgstr ""

#: 60b2d34b065845188bff819ea1ae072f
msgid ""
"Similarly, any understanding comes from a perspective, a particular "
"stand-point - which means that other perspectives and stand-points exist."
" **Explanation can and must consider alternatives**, counter-examples or "
"multiple different approaches to the same question."
msgstr ""

#: 10f7aa1134b54615b5c07eabe14b07df
msgid ""
"In explanation, you're not giving instruction or describing facts - "
"you're opening up the topic for consideration. It helps to think of "
"explanation as discussion: discussions can even consider and weigh up "
"contrary *opinions*."
msgstr ""

#: 4ac7034c2b704d8f95ae51f2bbe13237
msgid "Keep explanation closely bounded"
msgstr ""

#: d3bbff6d697446d59bb57f616cc30419
msgid ""
"One risk of explanation is that it tends to absorb other things. The "
"writer, intent on covering the topic, feels the urge to include "
"instruction or technical description related to it. But documentation "
"already has other places for these, and allowing them to creep in "
"interferes with the explanation itself, and removes them from view in the"
" correct place."
msgstr ""

#: f7f2dc3fb9da4683bcb0d6bdecaff3b4
msgid "The language of explanation"
msgstr ""

#: 17794efd18c545b984602dd4ac4e2afe
msgid "*The reason for x is because historically, y ...*"
msgstr ""

#: fcf33d9cd27e4e34b09af953ac7931c1
msgid "Explain."
msgstr ""

#: 8d5af337387d44a39bb04adfcc3ee457
msgid "*W is better than z, because ...*"
msgstr ""

#: 7795ab34b6db453e9aa6adbe9f3fb810
msgid "Offer judgements and even opinions where appropriate.."
msgstr ""

#: 40bbc2df97a3461fb46f2f1b54640315
msgid "*An x in system y is analogous to a w in system z. However ...*"
msgstr ""

#: 115ac6ac3d864ec9a898442a45e05105
msgid "Provide context that helps the reader."
msgstr ""

#: 2b0f0903ae8742b9b6fcf144f0fe084a
msgid "*Some users prefer w (because z). This can be a good approach, but...*"
msgstr ""

#: c62474c9713a4c6986827f7f8a6f53bc
msgid "Weigh up alternatives."
msgstr ""

#: 9fd8fe4d4471455e8f0fc50769f744c6
msgid "*An x interacts with a y as follows: ...*"
msgstr ""

#: d86ce82d24be4313bd76f53153fcad97
msgid ""
"Unfold the machinery's internal secrets, to help understand why something"
" does what it does."
msgstr ""

#: fcab665ed081413e9219403edfcf8e8e
msgid "Analogy from food and cooking"
msgstr ""

#: a91080002469451da035f50b80776279
msgid ""
"In 1984 `Harold McGee <https://www.curiouscook.com>`_ published *On food "
"and cooking*."
msgstr ""

#: 85271369753b4e4b8defcd31d5d45076
msgid ""
"The book doesn't teach how to cook anything. It doesn't contain recipes "
"(except as historical examples) and it isn't a work of reference. "
"Instead, it places food and cooking in the context of history, society, "
"science and technology. It explains for example why we do what we do in "
"the kitchen and how that has changed."
msgstr ""

#: 0dd787745e5248cab1c75e7f55b819a8
msgid ""
"It's clearly not a book we would read *while* cooking. We would read when"
" we want to reflect on cooking. It illuminates the subject by taking "
"multiple different perspectives on it, shining light from different "
"angles."
msgstr ""

#: 6bba909e369543a79952196c52766c23
msgid ""
"After reading a book like *On food and cooking*, our understanding is "
"changed. Our knowledge is richer and deeper. What we have learned may or "
"may not be immediately applicable next time we are doing something in the"
" kitchen, but *it will change how we think about our craft, and will "
"affect our practice*."
msgstr ""

